NT in raw .bin chunks → inaccurate seek position (sometimes works, sometimes off by seconds).\ndocs/video-streaming-report.md:970:2. **3MB chunk is large for progressive streaming** — 60s at 1Mbps video = 7.5MB total = 3 chunks to fetch. Prefetch latency (GitHub API ≈500ms/call per chunk range) means stall risk on slow WiFi. StreamVideo uses 4MB window prefetch; StreamVideoMSE uses 1MB + fragment index (better, if index exists).\ndocs/video-streaming-report.md:972:3. **No codec detection in manifest** — type:'chunked-media' omits 'codecs' field. MediaViewer (line 69) routes MSE only if type=='mse-av' (which includes codecs). Fallback StreamVideo relies on <video src> native probing (works for H.264/AAC but risky for VP9/Opus).\ndocs/video-streaming-report.md:974:4. **Separate shard vs. content repo routing** — manifest.repo field (StreamVideoMSE.jsx line 231, StreamVideo.jsx line 58) switches /api/stream between shard privé (token server-side) and public zenray-content. Adds routing layer; /api/stream already handles both (line 38), but manifest must declare repo correctly or chunks return 404.\ndocs/video-streaming-report.md:976:5. **No HLS/DASH fallback** — chunked-media + raw .bin requires Range support. If proxy/CDN doesn't support Range (rare but possible), streaming breaks. HLS (.m3u8 + .ts segments) is universally compatible; DASH (manifest.mpd + .m4s) is MP4-native.\ndocs/video-streaming-report.md:978:6. **Seek precision in fMP4 limited by fragment boundaries** — video-mse.mjs builds fragIndex (lines 106-124: walks moov/moof boxes, reads tfdt baseMediaDecodeTime). Fragments are ~3MB, so seek may be ±1.5MB off (seconds of video). Video-transcode.mjs (older pipeline) doesn't produce fragIndex → StreamVideoMSE degrades to linear approximation.\ndocs/video-streaming-report.md:986:  - Player handles seek backwards (StreamVideo detects, resets prefetch cursor)\ndocs/video-streaming-report.md:992:- Initial load: 512KB init (line 29 StreamVideoMSE) + 1st chunk ≈ 1-2